<title>NEW ZEALAND: NZ ADRs firmer in late New York, Dow up 16 points.</title>
<headline>NZ ADRs firmer in late New York, Dow up 16 points.</headline>
<dateline>WELLINGTON 1996-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>New Zealand ADRs were firmer in late New York trade, where the Dow Industrials Index was up 15.78 points at 6,742.66.</p>
<p>Price movements of NZ stocks listed in the U.S. and Britain at 7.40 a.m. (1840 GMT).</p>
<p>Company		   Exchange    Last	  Net change</p>
<p>FCL Bldg		    N.Y.    US$32 1/4	 +0 3/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Engy		    N.Y.    US$30 7/8	 +0 3/8 *</p>
<p>FCL Paper		   N.Y.    US$21 3/4	 +0 1/4 *</p>
<p>FCL Forest		  N.Y.    US$16 1/2	   nil  *</p>
<p>Telecom		     N.Y.    US$84 7/8	   nil  *</p>
<p>Tranz Rail		  N.Y.    untraded		   *</p>
<p>Guinness Peat	     London  33 1/2		nil</p>
<p>Brierley		    London  untraded</p>
<p>NZ IT			 London  untraded</p>
<p>Foreign &amp; Col	     London  151 3/4	   +0 1/4</p>
<p>Templeton		   London  146 1/4		+2</p>
<p>Lion Nathan		 Sydney  A$3.29		 +4</p>
<p>Goooman		     Sydney  A$1.61		nil</p>
<p>Macraes		     Sydney  A$2.64		 -6</p>
<p>Notes - In New York, Telecom's American Depository Receipts are traded in bundles of 16 shares, while both the Fletcher Challenge shares are in bundles of 10 each. Tranz Rail ADSs are groups of three ordinary shares.</p>
<p>- London prices are mid-rates.</p>
<p>- Asterisk * means stock is still trading</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom 64 4 4734 746</p>
</text>
